Require Vivado 2025.1 for the HDL project

The vendor HDL tree declares 2022.2 as its only supported Vivado release and
refuses to create a project under 2025.1 before synthesis starts.  The devkit
now pins its entire FPGA build flow to 2025.1, so make the upstream guard match
the toolchain the repository tests and publishes with.  This is a real version
requirement, not ADI_IGNORE_VERSION_CHECK: an accidental invocation of another
release must still stop before it emits an unreviewed bitstream.

diff --git a/hdl/scripts/adi_env.tcl b/hdl/scripts/adi_env.tcl
--- a/hdl/scripts/adi_env.tcl
+++ b/hdl/scripts/adi_env.tcl
@@ -13,3 +13,3 @@
# Define the supported tool version
-set required_vivado_version "2022.2"
+set required_vivado_version "2025.1"
 if {[info exists ::env(REQUIRED_VIVADO_VERSION)]} {
   set required_vivado_version $::env(REQUIRED_VIVADO_VERSION)
 } elseif {[info exists REQUIRED_VIVADO_VERSION]} {
